From: Kervin Pursoty <kpursoty@proton.me>
Subject: mips: econet: add EN751627 SoC Kconfig entry

The EN751627 family (EN7516, EN7527, EN7561) is a big-endian quad-VPE
MIPS 1004Kc SoC used in DSL/WiFi gateway devices such as the ZyXEL
EX3301-T0. It shares the MIPS GIC interrupt controller with EN7528 but
is big-endian and has four VPEs (NR_CPUS=4).

Key differences from existing SoCs:
- EN751221: BE, single-core 34Kc, custom INTC
- EN7528:   LE, dual-core 1004Kc, MIPS GIC
- EN751627: BE, quad-VPE 1004Kc, MIPS GIC

The SMP plumbing (CM/CPC probe + CPS SMP ops) is shared with EN7528 and
lives in patch 100 (device_tree_init). The earlycon timeout adjustment
lives in patch 103 (prom_init). This patch adds only the Kconfig entry.

Note: on EN751627, mips_cpc_probe() must be called before
register_cps_smp_ops(). Without it, core 1 never comes online because
write_gcr_co_reset_release(0) is insufficient on this SoC. This is
different from EN7528 where CPC probe behaves identically. Both SoCs
are covered by the shared #if in device_tree_init().

Signed-off-by: Kervin Pursoty <kpursoty@proton.me>
---
--- a/arch/mips/econet/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/econet/Kconfig
@@ -41,5 +41,29 @@ choice
 		  The EN7528 family with dual-core MIPS 1004Kc.
 		  Requires MIPS_RAW_APPENDED_DTB=y for boot.
+
+	config SOC_ECONET_EN751627
+		bool "EN751627 family"
+		select COMMON_CLK
+		select CPU_BIG_ENDIAN
+		select HAVE_PCI
+		select IRQ_MIPS_CPU
+		select MIPS_CM
+		select MIPS_CPC
+		select MIPS_CPS
+		select MIPS_CPU_SCACHE
+		select MIPS_GIC
+		select MIPS_MT_SMP
+		select PCI_DRIVERS_GENERIC
+		select SMP
+		select SMP_UP
+		select SYS_SUPPORTS_HIGHMEM
+		select SYS_SUPPORTS_MIPS_CPS
+		select SYS_SUPPORTS_MULTITHREADING
+		select SYS_SUPPORTS_SMP
+		help
+		  The EN751627 family (EN7516, EN7527, EN7561) with big-endian
+		  quad-VPE MIPS 1004Kc and MIPS GIC. Used in DSL+WiFi gateways.
+		  Requires MIPS_RAW_APPENDED_DTB=y for boot.
 endchoice
